# What a VSIX holds (scripts/package-vsix.mjs): everything is left out, then only what the
# installed extension reads is let back in. Sources, tests, node_modules (the extension is
# bundled by esbuild), source maps, the playground, caches and docs stay out.
**

!package.json
!README.md
!CHANGELOG.md
!LICENSE

!dist/extension.js
!dist/webview/*.js
!dist/webview/*.css
!dist/webview/land.geojson

!media/debrief.svg
!media/walkthroughs/**

# The Python bundled for this platform (scripts/bundle-python.mjs), without caches it might
# write if run before packaging; its .pyc files are compiled ahead and kept.
!python/**
python/**/*.pyc.*
python/**/*.whl
